# NOTES

## Structural findings

1. **Anachronistic "NPCIL" attribution across the pre-1987 fleet.** NPCIL (Nuclear Power Corporation of India Limited) was incorporated in 1987. Every reactor whose original construction predates 1987 -- Tarapur 1-2 (1969), Rajasthan 1-2 (1972/1981), Madras 1-2 (1984/1986), Narora 1-2 (1991, but construction began 1976-77) -- has "NPCIL" listed as constructor and/or architect_engineer in the source data. This is very likely a blanket retroactive label applied by the original heuristic rather than a period-accurate attribution. The correct period-accurate entity for the pre-1987 era is DAE (Department of Atomic Energy) or its operating arm, with AECL (Canada) directly involved for Rajasthan 1-2 and GE/Bechtel for Tarapur 1-2. Recommend a database-wide pass flagging any reactor with first-criticality/construction-start date before 1987 for constructor/AE re-review, not just the units in this batch.

2. **PFBR is not an NPCIL reactor.** It is owned/constructed by BHAVINI (a separate DAE public-sector undertaking created specifically for fast-breeder deployment) and designed by IGCAR, not NPCIL. This is a clear, high-confidence miscategorization likely caused by a heuristic that defaulted every Indian reactor to "NPCIL" regardless of reactor class. Recommend checking the full India dataset for any other fast-reactor or non-NPCIL entries (e.g. future FBR units) with the same default-NPCIL error.

3. **Turbine supplier and calandria/RPV manufacturer are systematically undocumented for standard Indian PHWRs.** Across every "standard" indigenous unit checked (Kaiga, Kakrapar 1-2, Rajasthan 3-8, Tarapur 3-4), no citable per-unit source could be found naming BHEL as turbine supplier or L&T as calandria fabricator, despite this being widely understood industry practice. These fields are marked UNVERIFIABLE (not CONFIRMED) throughout this batch per the "never bless a plausible guess" instruction. A future verification pass should target NPCIL annual reports, BHEL/L&T press releases, or IAEA PRIS per-unit component pages (not reachable via WebFetch in this session) rather than Wikipedia, which does not carry this level of detail.

4. **Kakrapar 3/4 BHEL-Alstom turbine claim remains unresolved.** The prior sample finding that flagged this as a known correction could not be independently corroborated or refuted with a citable source in this session -- it is carried forward as UNVERIFIABLE, not CONFIRMED, pending a source with WebSearch access to NPCIL press releases, L&T/BHEL annual reports, or World Nuclear News archives.

5. **Pakistan: CNNC is a parent-holding-company label, not the precise EPC contractor.** For Chashma 3/4/Karachi 2/3, the documented general contractor is CZEC (China Zhongyuan Engineering Corporation), a CNNC subsidiary -- not "CNNC" itself. Chashma 1/2/5 could not be confirmed either way (WNA's Pakistan profile is less explicit about the contractor for these units) and are marked UNVERIFIABLE rather than assumed to follow the same CZEC pattern.

6. **Karachi 2/3 architect_engineer is likely NOT SNERDI.** The 2013 contract-signing announcement names CNPE and NPIC as the Chinese design-side entities for the HPR1000 export units, not SNERDI (which is documented for the earlier CNP-300 Chashma units). The original heuristic appears to have copy-pasted "SNERDI" across all Pakistani reactors regardless of design generation.

7. **KANUPP (Karachi 1) constructor/architect_engineer were swapped in the source data.** The documented split is: Montreal Engineering Company as the civil construction contractor, General Electric Canada (Canadian General Electric) as the design/turnkey contractor -- i.e. closer to an AE role than the guessed "AECL" for both fields.

8. **Research constraint:** both verification sub-agents exhausted their WebSearch budget mid-task and had to fall back on WebFetch against known URLs (primarily Wikipedia and the WNA India/Pakistan country profiles). Turbine-supplier and RPV/calandria-manufacturer fields are the least-verifiable category across this entire batch as a direct result -- a follow-up pass with fresh search budget targeting NPCIL/BHEL/L&T press releases and World Nuclear News/Nuclear Engineering International archives would likely resolve many of the 78 UNVERIFIABLE rows below.
